{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Hockenhull, Michael","Maguire, James","Figueiredo, Felipe Silva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776451"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Climate","It","Quality of Life"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reset a climate magazine by the it university of copenhagen living well with technology in the climate emergency","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106988465/1094320_Reset_magazine_III_2024_FINAL.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funded and published by the Center for Climate IT"],"id":"S01-000.00-776451","ids":["itu-db0469d9-68d8-46f4-98b0-f6664e4eec63"],"keyword":["IT","Quality of life","climate"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3C99758CF259B50188CF9C577C4F012D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106988465/1094320_Reset_magazine_III_2024_FINAL.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, ETHOS Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"hockenhullpau","last":"Hockenhull","locid":"5041f387-908f-4845-9f79-3a6dbd527f4b","name":"Hockenhull, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-2670-2102","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"maguirepau","last":"Maguire","locid":"2efbc294-1ce4-4148-a403-93fe6450d879","name":"Maguire, James","orcid":"0000-0001-5081-1811","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Felipe Silva","key":"figueiredopau","last":"Figueiredo","locid":"c3ca425d-f0d9-493b-9012-7dee3b9e2dfb","name":"Figueiredo, Felipe Silva","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-db0469d9-68d8-46f4-98b0-f6664e4eec63"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"RESET - A climate magazine by the IT University of Copenhagen : Living well with technology in the climate emergency?","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776451","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Mammalian carnivores are considered a key group in maintaining ecological health and can indicate potential ecological integrity in landscapes where they occur. Carnivores also hold high conservation value and their habitat requirements can guide management and conservation plans. The order Carnivora has 84 species from 8 families in the Neotropical region: Canidae; Felidae; Mephitidae; Mustelidae; Otariidae; Phocidae; Procyonidae; and Ursidae. Herein, we include published and unpublished data on native terrestrial Neotropical carnivores (Canidae; Felidae; Mephitidae; Mustelidae; Procyonidae; and Ursidae). NEOTROPICAL CARNIVORES is a publicly available data set that includes 99,605 data entries from 35,511 unique georeferenced coordinates. Detection/non-detection and quantitative data were obtained from 1818 to 2018 by researchers, governmental agencies, non-governmental organizations, and private consultants. Data were collected using several methods including camera trapping, museum collections, roadkill, line transect, and opportunistic records. Literature (peer-reviewed and grey literature) from Portuguese, Spanish and English were incorporated in this compilation. Most of the data set consists of detection data entries (n = 79,343; 79.7%) but also includes non-detection data (n = 20,262; 20.3%). Of those, 43.3% also include count data (n = 43,151). The information available in NEOTROPICAL CARNIVORES will contribute to macroecological, ecological, and conservation questions in multiple spatio-temporal perspectives. As carnivores play key roles in trophic interactions, a better understanding of their distribution and habitat requirements are essential to establish conservation management plans and safeguard the future ecological health of Neotropical ecosystems. Our data paper, combined with other large-scale data sets, has great potential to clarify species distribution and related ecological processes within the Neotropics. There are no copyright restrictions and no restriction for using data from this data paper, as long as the data paper is cited as the source of the information used. We also request that users inform us of how they intend to use the data.","author_count":694,"contributors":["Nagy-Reis, Mariana","Oshima, Júlia Emi de Faria","Kanda, Claudia Zukeran","Palmeira, Francesca Belem Lopes","de Melo, Fabiano Rodrigues","Morato, Ronaldo Gonçalves","Bonjorne, Lilian","Magioli, Marcelo","Leuchtenberger, Caroline","Rohe, Fabio","Lemos, Frederico Gemesio","Martello, Felipe","Alves-Eigenheer, Milene","da Silva, Rafaela Aparecida","Silveira dos Santos, Juliana","Priante, Camila Fátima","Bernardo, Rodrigo","Rogeri, Patricia","Assis, Julia Camara","Gaspar, Lucas Pacciullio","Tonetti, Vinicius Rodrigues","Trinca, Cristiano Trapé","Ribeiro, Adauto de Souza","Bocchiglieri, Adriana","Hass, Adriani","Canteri, Adriano","Chiarello, Adriano Garcia","Paglia, Adriano Pereira","Pereira, Adriele Aparecida","de Souza, Agnis Cristiane","Gatica, Ailin","Medeiro, Akyllam Zoppi","Eriksson, Alan","Costa, Alan Nilo","González-Gallina, Alberto","Yanosky, Alberto A.","Jesus de la Cruz, Alejandro","Bertassoni, Alessandra","Bager, Alex","Bovo, Alex Augusto Abreu","Cravino Mol, Alexandra","Bezerra, Alexandra Maria Ramos","Percequillo, Alexandre","Vogliotti, Alexandre","Costa Lopes, Alexandre Martins","Keuroghlian, Alexine","Zúñiga Hartley, Alfonso Christopher","Devlin, Allison L.","de Paula, Almir","García-Olaechea, Alvaro","Sánchez, Amadeo","Aquino, Ana Carla Medeiros Morato","Srbek-Araujo, Ana Carolina","Ochoa, Ana Cecilia","Tomazzoni, Ana Cristina","Lacerda, Ana Cristyna Reis","Bacellar, Ana Elisa de Faria","Campelo, Ana Kellen Nogueira","Herrera Victoria, Ana María","Paschoal, Ana Maria de Oliveira","Potrich, Ana Paula","Gomes, Ana Paula Nascimento","Olímpio, Ana Priscila Medeiros","Cunha Costa, Ana Raissa","Jácomo, Anah Tereza de Almeida","Calaça, Analice Maria","Jesus, Anamélia Souza","de Barros Barban, Ananda","Feijó, Anders